Z||000000||firstfiero||04-29-2001||02:02 AM||||    Well I replace the thermostat today but it's still over heating. I figured out today that it only starts to overheat when sitting still and by reving the engine it immediatly starts to cool. My water pump looks fine..my fan belt is dry rotted and has chunks out of it? Could this be the culprit. Maybe its slipping and at idle its not turning it fast enough to move the water...but when I rev the engine it gets the water flowing. <BR>   Another qustion....do the arrows have to go the whole way forward when putting the cap back over the thermostat. I just about broke my hand getting it back half way. <BR>   I'm taking it in tomorrow morning to have a new fan belt put on...Is their a sensor I should have them look at?   Thanks for any help....<P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif"> <BR>Todd <BR>  86se||||reg||8
Z||000001||Spektyr||04-29-2001||07:18 AM||||I know what you're talking about with the thermo cap... I damn near killed myself trying to get it on and off.  Then I read here about using an oil filter wrench to do it.  Sounds smart as long as you don't manage to mangle the cap (in other words, do it carefully).<P>As for the overheating... the fan belt is possible, but my gut says not likely.  Possible culprits that come to mind:<P>- Poor flow due to kinked or clogged lines, clogged radiator, pump about to fail.<BR>- Air in the system, but I would think that you wouldn't get the rev cooling you describe with that problem.<P>I'd check all the lines for any evidence of denting, age, etc.  One indication that the waterpump is going out is any play in the waterpump pully.  I had an old Pontiac Parisienne that suddenly threw three fan blades and then 1 mile later puked the water pump (right in the driveway, the neighbors were un-thrilled).  Sure enough the water pump shaft was wobbly as hell.  (that's what threw the fan blades)  If the main bearing starts to go, that's pretty much your only warning.  Sometimes it will squeal, sometimes not.<P>I'm sure someone else can think of something I'm forgetting here.<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)<BR>--Um, no the paint isn't oxidized, that's the ultra-rare Whirlpool White textured finish... yeah.<BR>89 Lincoln Town Car (has Fiero Envy)<BR>--Hey!  Can I have an anti-sway bar too?||||reg||1
